{
  "dom_id": "step-q50029",
  "name": "Question 1",
  "problem": "A cat’s position relative to a fixed origin $O$ is given by the function $x(t)=3{t}^{2}+t$ meters, where $t$ is the time in hours. Find the average position of the cat between $2$ and $4$ hours.",
  "worked_solution": "To calculate the average value of the position on $[{t}_{1},{t}_{2}],$ we use the average value formula\n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{{t}_{2}-{t}_{1}}\\,{\\int }_{{t}_{1}}^{{t}_{2}}x(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{4-2}\\,{\\int }_{2}^{4}(3{t}^{2}+t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{({t}^{3}+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{2})|}_{2}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[({4}^{3}+\\frac{{4}^{2}}{2})-({2}^{3}+\\frac{{2}^{2}}{2})] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[(64+8)-(8+2)] \\\\  & =31.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the average position is $31\\,\\text{m}.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
